paragraph start
name: paragraph-aiu-notation-is
AIU NOTATION is a plain text format for pages. A page is a file
ending in .aiu, made of blocks. One source is read many ways: as
boxes, as rich text, as plain text, by checks and by a database.
contract start
id: q94fc72
question: Does the paragraph make one point?
contract end
answer start
for: q94fc72
asked: Does the paragraph make one point?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-two-programs-read
Two programs read the same pages. The notation binary in Rust
holds the parser, the views and the database. The Racket model
holds the outline, numbering, page types and checks. The editor
aiutd builds against the Rust crate by path.
