code start
name: code-code-text-the
language: text
code  |  text the parser does not read as notation  |  yes
comment  |  a block of text the reader drops  |  no
contents  |  the table of contents, computed from the chapter tree  |  no
contract  |  the question text copied from its file, read only  |  no
copyright  |  the copyright page of a book  |  no
cover  |  the cover of a book, title and author only  |  no
figure  |  a figure with a caption  |  no
footnote  |  a note shown at the foot of the page that cites it  |  no
header  |  the header row of a table  |  no
index  |  the index of terms, computed from the tree  |  no
paragraph  |  ordinary prose, the everyday case  |  no
preface  |  the preface of a book  |  no
reference  |  one cited source, collected by the bibliography  |  no
row  |  one row of a table  |  no
table  |  a table of rows  |  no
title-page  |  the title page of a book  |  no
title  |  a heading that names the file  |  no
volume  |  one volume of a book that has several  |  no
list  |  items, one per line, drawn with bullets  |  no
steps  |  ordered actions, one per line, drawn numbered  |  no
definition  |  a term and its meaning, first line is the term  |  no
example  |  a worked example, first line is its name  |  no
exercise  |  a task for the reader, first line is its name  |  no
space  |  blank room for hand work, first line is the line count  |  no
formula  |  an equation, text the parser does not read  |  yes
callout  |  a boxed remark, first line is note, warning or tip  |  no
pin  |  keeps its blocks on screen, first line is top or bottom, then write or read, then hide  |  no
